# Non-secret environment for the `recorder` Docker Compose service ONLY.
# Copy to deploy/recorder.env on the server (see deploy/SERVER_SETUP.md section 13),
# alongside (not instead of) the repo-root .env created from .env.example.
#
# Deliberately does NOT hold TBOT_TABDEAL_API_KEY / TBOT_TABDEAL_API_SECRET /
# TBOT_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN / TBOT_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID (fix-round finding, minor #5): the
# recorder only calls Tabdeal's PUBLIC endpoints (/trades, /depth), which need no
# signing at all (tbot.execution.tabdeal_client.TabdealClient works with
# api_key=None/api_secret=None for exactly these calls), so it has no business holding
# exchange credentials — not in its environment, not in `docker inspect tbot-recorder`
# output, not reachable by anyone in the server's `docker` group. Those secrets live
# only in the repo-root `.env`, reserved for services that are actually going to sign
# requests (the Telegram bot / TabdealBroker, phase 5+), and are never passed to this
# container (see the `env_file:` comment on the `recorder` service in
# deploy/docker-compose.yml).
#
# Intentionally empty otherwise today: TBOT_CONFIG and TZ are already set directly in
# docker-compose.yml's `environment:` block for this service, so there is nothing else
# the recorder needs yet. This file exists so the recorder has somewhere non-secret to
# grow into, without ever reaching for the root .env.
